---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const body = "<section class=\"hero wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">// Services</span><span class=\"folio\">01</span></div> </div> <h1 class=\"h1 reveal d1\" style=\"max-width:22ch;margin-top:18px;font-size:clamp(32px,4.4vw,60px)\">Landing Pages — One Page, One Decision</h1> <p class=\"lead reveal d2\" style=\"margin-top:22px\">A single page with one job: getting the right person to take one clear action.</p> <div class=\"reveal d3\" style=\"margin-top:32px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <a href=\"https://wa.me/6285927277560?text=Hi!%20I'd%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20landing%20page...\" class=\"btn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-wa=\"hero\" data-page=\"/en/services/landing-page-design.html\"> Free Consultation<span class=\"arr\">↗</span> </a> <a href=\"/en/pricing\" class=\"btn ghost\">See pricing <span class=\"arr\">↗</span></a> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 02 — The problem</span><span class=\"folio\">02</span></div> </div> <div class=\"persp\"> <div class=\"reveal\"><p class=\"big\">Landing pages fail because they are asked to do too much.</p></div> <div class=\"reveal d1\"> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">A landing page that does not work almost always has the same symptom: a &quot;Sign Up&quot; button at the top, and also a menu to nine other pages, a link to the blog, social icons, and a newsletter form at the bottom. Every one of those is an exit from the decision you actually want.</p><p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">A landing page is not a short website. It is closer to an argument: why this person, today, should do this thing. Everything that does not strengthen the argument weakens it.</p><p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-bottom:20px\">So the first conversation is not about design. It is about one sentence: who lands here, from where, and what is the single thing they should do? If the answer has more than one item, a landing page is not what you need.</p> </div> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 03 — What's included</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px;max-width:20ch\">What you actually get.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">03</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"deflist reveal\"> <div><b>Offer sharpening</b><p>A session to lock one goal, one audience, one action. Often the part that changes the result most.</p></div><div><b>Argument structure</b><p>Message order from promise to proof to objection to ask — agreed before design.</p></div><div><b>Design &amp; build</b><p>One page, fast and light. Load speed is part of conversion, not a bonus.</p></div><div><b>Mobile-first</b><p>Most ad traffic arrives on a phone. It gets designed there first.</p></div><div><b>Conversion tracking</b><p>Events wired from the start, so you know whether it works instead of guessing.</p></div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 04 — Fit</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px;max-width:22ch\">Who this is for — and who it isn't.</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">The right column matters as much as the left. I would rather lose the project here than have us both discover it in week five.</p> </div> <span class=\"folio\">04</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"fit-grid reveal\"> <div class=\"fit yes\"><b>A good fit if</b><ul><li>Paid campaigns that need a focused destination.</li><li>Product, course, or event launches with a fixed date.</li><li>Testing a new offer before building a full site.</li><li>Businesses with traffic but no action.</li></ul></div> <div class=\"fit no\"><b>Not a fit if</b><ul><li>You need somewhere to explain the whole company. That is a company profile.</li><li>You have more than one goal. Two goals on one page means zero.</li><li>You are hoping the page fixes an offer that is not compelling yet. It sharpens an argument; it cannot invent one.</li><li>You have no plan to drive traffic. Landing pages do not generate visitors.</li></ul></div> </div> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 05 — Process</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">How this runs.</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">1–2 weeks if the offer and content are clear. Sharpening the offer is what usually adds time.</p> </div> <span class=\"folio\">05</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"proc\"> <div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">1.</div><h3>Sharpen the offer</h3><p>One audience, one goal, one action. If this cannot be locked, there is no point continuing.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">2.</div><h3>Argument structure</h3><p>Message order agreed as an outline before design — far cheaper to argue about at this stage.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">3.</div><h3>Design &amp; build</h3><p>One page, fast, mobile-first, with tracking in place.</p></div><div class=\"proc-step reveal\"><div class=\"pn\">4.</div><h3>Launch &amp; measure</h3><p>Shipped with conversion events that actually fire, so the next decision has data behind it.</p></div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div> <span class=\"eyebrow\">// 06 — Pricing</span> <h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">By consultation</h2> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:16px;max-width:62ch\">Typically below the company profile package. Depends on page length and integration needs.</p> <div style=\"margin-top:26px\"><a href=\"/en/pricing\" class=\"btn ghost\">Full pricing &amp; what's excluded <span class=\"arr\">↗</span></a></div> </div> <span class=\"folio\">06</span> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 07 — Examples</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">Comparable work.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">07</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"more-grid reveal\"> <a class=\"more-card\" href=\"https://indycar-fleet-hub.lovable.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> <div class=\"mthumb\"><img src=\"/img/work/nusantara-rent.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot of the Nusantara Rent project\" width=\"1200\" height=\"555\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div> <div class=\"mt\"><h3 class=\"h3\">Nusantara Rent</h3><span class=\"mtag\">.Creator .Lovable</span></div> <p>A car rental service with drivers operating across cities. The challenge: a fleet spanning family Avanzas to VVIP Alphards had to read clearly in one screen without making anyone feel they were in the wrong place. I built a dark-and-gold hierarchy that leads with capacity and price, then cut the booking path down to a single step into WhatsApp.</p> <span class=\"open\">View site ↗</span> </a><a class=\"more-card\" href=\"https://www.thearisefoundation.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> <div class=\"mthumb\"><img src=\"/img/work/the-arise-foundation.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot of the The Arise Foundation project\" width=\"945\" height=\"816\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div> <div class=\"mt\"><h3 class=\"h3\">The Arise Foundation</h3><span class=\"mtag\">.Wix Studio .Gamify</span></div> <p>A youth-driven initiative in Tanzania. The challenge: a gamified quiz for students. I told their impact story through specific outcomes — 1,300 lunches a day, 100 laptops — turning a sense of connection into donor action.</p> <span class=\"open\">View site ↗</span> </a> </div> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:24px;font-size:15px\"> <a href=\"/en/work\" style=\"text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px\">See the full portfolio</a> — with the reasoning behind each decision.\n</p> </section> <hr class=\"hair\" style=\"margin:0 var(--gut)\"> <section class=\"pad-sm wrap\"> <div class=\"shead reveal\"> <div class=\"label\"> <div><span class=\"eyebrow\">// 08 — Questions</span><h2 class=\"h2\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">What people usually ask.</h2></div> <span class=\"folio\">08</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"faq reveal\"> <details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/01</span>How is this different from a page on my website?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">A normal page lives inside navigation and invites exploration. A landing page deliberately removes every exit so only one decision makes sense. Technically both are pages; in purpose they are opposites.</p> </details><details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/02</span>Can it live on my existing domain?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">Yes, usually as a subdirectory or subdomain. If your site already has authority, keeping it on the same domain is generally better than a separate one.</p> </details><details> <summary><span class=\"fq\">/03</span>Do you manage the ads too?</summary> <p class=\"fa\">No. Google Ads and Meta Ads are not my service. I build the destination and make sure measurement is correct; ad management belongs with someone who does it daily.</p> </details> </div> </section> <section class=\"cta-ink pad\"> <img class=\"bgimg\" src=\"/img/cta-bg.webp\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1024\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\"> <div class=\"wrap\" style=\"position:relative\"> <span class=\"eyebrow reveal\">// Let's talk</span> <h2 class=\"h2 reveal d1\" style=\"margin:24px 0 36px;max-width:20ch\">Sounds like a fit? Let's test that first.</h2> <div class=\"reveal d2\"> <a href=\"https://wa.me/6285927277560?text=Hi!%20I'd%20like%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20landing%20page...\" class=\"btn on-ink\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-wa=\"cta\" data-page=\"/en/services/landing-page-design.html\"> Free Consultation<span class=\"arr\">↗</span> </a> </div> </div> </section>";
const extraSchema = [{"@type":"Service","name":"landing page design service","description":"Landing pages with one goal and one decision. For campaigns, launches, and paid traffic that needs somewhere focused to land.","url":"https://mglportfolio.vercel.app/en/services/landing-page-design","serviceType":"Landing Page","provider":{"@id":"https://mglportfolio.vercel.app/#service"},"areaServed":{"@type":"Country","name":"Indonesia"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://mglportfolio.vercel.app/en"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://mglportfolio.vercel.app/en/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Landing Page","item":"https://mglportfolio.vercel.app/en/services/landing-page-design"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from a page on my website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A normal page lives inside navigation and invites exploration. A landing page deliberately removes every exit so only one decision makes sense. Technically both are pages; in purpose they are opposites."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can it live on my existing domain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, usually as a subdirectory or subdomain. If your site already has authority, keeping it on the same domain is generally better than a separate one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you manage the ads too?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Google Ads and Meta Ads are not my service. I build the destination and make sure measurement is correct; ad management belongs with someone who does it daily."}}]}];
